# Q4 – Choosing a Map for a Pharmacy Inventory

---

## 1. Initial Predictions & Theoretical Expectations

| Map Type | Expected `put` Cost | Expected `get` Cost | Iteration Cost | Natural Report Output |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`HashMap`** | $O(1)$ Average | $O(1)$ Average | $O(N + \text{capacity})$ | Unordered / Random |
| **`TreeMap`** | $O(\log N)$ | $O(\log N)$ | $O(N)$ | Sorted by Medicine Code |
| **`LinkedHashMap`** | $O(1)$ Average | $O(1)$ Average | $O(N)$ | Insertion Order |

### Extra Work for "Wrong" Map Choices
* If **`HashMap`** is used for the Code-Ordered report, entries must be extracted into a `List` and sorted using `Collections.sort()` costing $O(N \log N)$ extra time and space.
* If **`HashMap`** is used for the Insertion-Ordered report, order cannot be recovered unless an auxiliary history list is maintained.

